---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE, href, appVersion } from "../lib/site";
import { softwareApp, breadcrumbs } from "../lib/schema";
const version = appVersion();
const xattr = "xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/nekotrail.app";
const deb = "sudo apt install ./nekotrail_*_amd64.deb";
---
<Base
  title="Download for Mac and Linux"
  description="Download NekoTrail for Mac (Apple silicon and Intel) or Linux (.deb). Free, open source (MIT), no account. Runs 16 coding agents in parallel."
  path="download/"
  jsonld={[softwareApp(), breadcrumbs([["Home", ""], ["Download", "download/"]])]}
>
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>Download NekoTrail</h1>
      <p class="lede">Free, no account. Latest: v{version}. It updates itself.</p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="mac">
      <h2 id="mac" class="dl-title">Mac</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3>Download and drag to Applications</h3>
            <p>One .dmg for Apple silicon and Intel. macOS 13+.</p>
            <a class="btn primary" href={SITE.releases} rel="noopener" style="margin-top:12px">Download .dmg</a>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3>Run this once in Terminal</h3>
            <div class="copy-row">
              <pre><code>{xattr}</code></pre>
              <button class="copy-btn" type="button" data-copy={xattr}>Copy</button>
            </div>
            <p>Needed until the app is notarized by Apple.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3>Open NekoTrail</h3>
            <p>It checks your setup and offers the <a href={href("moving-from-conductor/")}>Conductor import</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="linux" style="margin-top:72px">
      <h2 id="linux" class="dl-title">Linux <span class="pill">Experimental</span></h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3>Install the .deb</h3>
            <div class="copy-row">
              <pre><code>{deb}</code></pre>
              <button class="copy-btn" type="button" data-copy={deb}>Copy</button>
            </div>
            <p>Debian, Ubuntu and similar, x86_64, glibc 2.35+. Other distros: <a href={`${SITE.repo}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`} rel="noopener">build from source</a> for now; the AppImage is paused.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3>Report what breaks</h3>
            <p>Linux is new. <a href={SITE.issues} rel="noopener">Open an issue</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <p class="muted" style="margin-top:72px">You also need at least one agent CLI, signed in with your own account. Gemini CLI signs in with a Gemini API key, Vertex AI or a Gemini Code Assist plan; Google says free-tier and Google One users moved to Antigravity CLI on 18 June 2026 (<a href="https://www.geminicli.com/docs/resources/tos-privacy" rel="noopener">Google's terms</a>).</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:24px 0 96px">Prefer to build it? See the <a href={`${SITE.repo}#install`} rel="noopener">README</a>. What changed: <a href={href("changelog/")}>changelog</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
